{"name":"Dutch Cocoa","hex":"#8c706a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dutch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["wife"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Dutch (“treat cocoa with alkali”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dutch"},{"term":"cocoa","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The dried and partially fermented fatty seeds of the cacao tree from which chocolate is made.","An unsweetened brown powder made from roasted, ground cocoa beans, used in making chocolate, and in cooking."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light to medium brown colour, like that of cocoa powder."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cocoa"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dutch process cocoa","blocks":[{"text":"Dutch processed cocoa, Dutched cocoa, or alkalized cocoa, is made from cocoa that has been treated with an alkalizing agent to reduce the natural acidity of cocoa, making it less bitter and darker compared to natural cocoa extracted with the Broma process. Alkalizing agents employed vary, but include potassium carbonate, sodium carbonate, and sodium hydroxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Dutch_process_and_natural_cocoa.jpg/330px-Dutch_process_and_natural_cocoa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dutch_process_cocoa"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"dutch":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/En-uk-Dutch.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f0/En-uk-Dutch.ogg/En-uk-Dutch.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d4/En-us-Dutch.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"htt